# M2 walkthrough: departments, versioned agents, the tool catalog, delegation.
# Works with the VS Code "REST Client" extension or the JetBrains HTTP client.
# Prerequisite: a provider and the default model role (see m1-providers.http).
# For the web tools: docker compose up -d searxng crawl4ai (CRAWL4AI_API_TOKEN set in .env).

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:4111
@token = paste-your-admin-token-here

### Tools an agent can be granted
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/catalog/tools
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Create a department
# @name department
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/departments
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "slug": "research", "name": "Research", "description": "Finds and summarizes information from the web." }

### Its lead. A lead's team is the department's specialists (delegation tools agent-<key>).
# @name lead
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "research-lead",
  "name": "Research lead",
  "role": "lead",
  "departmentId": "{{department.response.body.id}}",
  "description": "Plans research and reviews findings.",
  "instructions": "Delegate web lookups to the web researcher. Answer in at most five sentences.",
  "tools": [{ "key": "current_time" }]
}

### A specialist with the web tools
# @name specialist
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "key": "web-researcher",
  "name": "Web researcher",
  "role": "specialist",
  "departmentId": "{{department.response.body.id}}",
  "description": "Searches the web and reads pages; returns facts with source URLs.",
  "instructions": "Use web_search first, then fetch_page on the best result. Always list sources.",
  "tools": [{ "key": "web_search" }, { "key": "fetch_page" }]
}

### Both are live right away
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/agents
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Ask the lead: it delegates to the specialist, who searches the web
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agents/research-lead/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "What is the Mastra framework? Give one source URL." }] }

### Edit the specialist: creates and activates version 2, applies to the next run
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/v1/agents/{{specialist.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "instructions": "Use web_search, then summarize in two bullet points with sources." }

### Version history
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/agents/{{specialist.response.body.id}}/versions
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Roll back to version 1
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/agents/{{specialist.response.body.id}}/versions/1/activate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### The chief of staff knows the organization
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/agents/chief/generate
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "messages": [{ "role": "user", "content": "Which department can research things for me?" }] }

### The department with its lead and team
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/departments/{{department.response.body.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
